# Specialized subagent dispatch

When the user reports a HUD/API observation, bug, or polish request during testing:

1. Read skill **`jarvis-observation-dispatch`** (roster + prompt template).
2. Launch the matching agent from `.cursor/agents/` via Task:
   - UI/UX, layout, React Bits, cards, scroll, weather → **`jarvis-uiux`**
   - Speak, TTS, Voicebox, double-play, latency → **`jarvis-voice`**
   - Mail, HITL, RFQ, calendar, tools, Hermes routing → **`jarvis-workflows`**
   - Agreed implementation / restarts / verify → **`jarvis-builder`**
3. Set `run_in_background: true` unless the user asks to wait.
4. Use `subagent_type` matching the agent file name (`jarvis-uiux`, etc.).
5. Never invent a one-off agent when a roster specialist exists.
6. Parent chat stays on capability testing; agents report DONE/FILES/TRY/GAPS.
